The fix for crbug 535344406 (restricted: "Properly count transform feedback
struct varyings."): ANGLE main commit feb60947a1bfd2d92a3eadbe3f036795b427f740,
merged to ANGLE's 159 branch (chromium/8154) as
f55978a48d1c79fb70bea6c60cdf6f20d06ebb8a. No merge to ANGLE's 158 branch
(chromium/8127) has been proposed; 158's DEPS pins ANGLE at eae431b4e9b9.

VaryingPacking::collectTFVarying() packed every member of a struct only for
shader I/O blocks, and packVaryingIntoRegisterMap() let 1- to 3-component
struct or I/O block fields wrap into columns 1..3 of the register map once
column 0 had filled maxVaryingVectors rows. So a WebGL 2 program using
transform feedback with struct varyings could get more varyings packed than
the limits allow: a GPU-process issue reachable from web content.

This is the main commit's change to src/libANGLE/VaryingPacking.{cpp,h}
without its tests (VaryingPacking_unittest.cpp, TransformFeedbackTest.cpp),
regenerated against 158's ANGLE so it applies without offsets; the hunks are
main's. Drop this once 158's ANGLE includes the fix (check that the merged
change is the same).

